omx-dsp (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * packaging: omx-contract floor 2.14.0
  * bus sum: accumulate takes a non-finite coefficient as 0, with a value arm
    and sabotage (#170)
  * bus sum: say accumulate takes a non-finite coefficient as 0 (#170)
  * drive oracle: run the nine RME rates and assert the declared mark at each
    (#68)
  * drive oracle: declare the alias floor and stage peak marks per rate, with
    the measured reason (#68)
  * Ship omx-dsp-copy-check.1 and list the check's files in CI
  * omx-dsp-copy-check: find pow(10, x / 20) and pow(10, x / 2000)
  * omx-dsp-copy-check: the exports file and the check that reads it
  * Tag each function's TypeScript twin with @twin
  * contract-single-source: also name guards and #undef on a contract name
  * face-conformance: the delay tap controls and the graphic EQ mode are
    newer than the faces (#165)
  * oversampler: OMX_OVS_LATENCY_4X reads the contract's
    OMX_DETECTOR_OVERSAMPLE_LATENCY_SAMPLES (omx-contract#44)
  * align: OMX_ALIGN_MAX_MS reads the contract's
    OMX_INPUT_ALIGN_DELAY_RANGE_MAX (omx-contract#44)
  * hrp: OMX_HRP_HARMONICS reads the contract's OMX_HRP_HARMONIC_COUNT
    (omx-contract#44)
  * delay: the tap ceiling and the tap factor set from omx-contract
    (omx-contract#63)
  * omx_mbcomp: take the multiband limits from omx-contract (omx-contract#62)
  * Version 0.21.0: the mix maths, the multiband compressor and the pole law
    live in the library
  * test: break the strip alignment stage five ways and require its oracle to
    see each
  * ci: give the make test job 60 minutes, the suite runs 20 to 30
  * omx_dyn: seed y[n-1] when the slot enters the feedback loop (#78)
  * omxdsp.h includes omx_align.h; a check that every public header is
    reached or listed (#74)
  * release-arm-gate-selftest: gate() evaluates the parsed literals, with a
    sabotage run (#85)
  * denormal: guard the flush-to-zero effect checks on SSE float maths (#126)
  * contract-single-source: the self-test edits a scratch copy of the header
    (#108)
  * Refuse attribution lines in commit messages: commit-msg hook and a
    pull request check
  * public-sources-check: also scan the commit messages a pull request adds
  * omx_pole_rescale: a NaN rate is a rate the caller could not supply, and
    the pole stays in [0, 1]
  * mix goldens: the rest of the mix maths, written by the engine's own copies
  * mix/omx_route_gain: an output route's fill, fold and fold-fill gain stages
  * mix/omx_meter: omx_meter_strip_peak, the strip's post-fader reading
  * mix/omx_mix_coef: omx_mix_strip_split and omx_mix_settled_silent
  * mix/omx_pan_law: OMX_PAN_LCR_FOLD_CLEV, the LCR downmix's centre level
  * note-map-sabotage: twelve sabotages of omx_note_map.h, each red on the
    note_map arm (#150)
  * omx_note_map: a note leg's channel filter, key split, transpose and
    velocity curve (#150)
  * test/fx: band_dyn_poly-perturb.sh, a sabotage per arm of the poly oracle
  * omx_band_dyn: gain path on the libm-free unit pair, in 64-sample chunks
  * tools: deesser-cost.c, the de-esser's ns per frame by the plugin cost
    method
  * test/fx: hold the band-dynamics loop to its libm form, frozen verbatim
  * omx_units: state omx_lin_to_db_poly's bound over every float level
  * omxdsp_threads: the gate joins the 8-thread identity arm
  * omx_env_step: the cascade picks its one-pole's result, not its pole
  * gate cost: a bench for the gate kernel and a base-against-tree A/B
  * delay-taps-sabotage: the tap oracle sees six broken kernels
  * fx delay: up to four integer read taps on the one ring
  * pole-rescale-guard: one home for the reference-rate pole law
  * onepole-sabotage: the rescale checks see four broken copies
  * delay tone, reverb damping: the poles call omx_pole_rescale
  * omx_pole_rescale: a reference-rate pole at the running rate
  * geq true oracle: a clamped gain keeps its target's sign, and a seventh
    sabotage proves the arm sees it (#129)
  * mbcomp oracle: keep the running maxima as comparisons, not fmax over
    widened floats (#128)
  * fx: mbcomp-perturb, five sabotages the multiband oracle must see (#128)
  * fx: omx_mbcomp, a multiband compressor over an LR4 crossover tree (#128)
  * geq true mode: oracle at the nine RME rates and six sabotages (#129)
  * geq instance: true mode, the two-pass gain solve as a control-thread
    design (#129)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:10:37 +0000
